{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And the men took this present.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): the reason he mentioned them by the name 'men' and not by the name 'brothers' is to indicate their going with great zeal, like men. And furthermore, because they were entering the land in great fear and were disguising themselves, so that no one would recognize them as brothers but rather as strangers." "<b>And by way of the Kabbalah</b>, the term 'men' alludes to the ten slain of the kingdom (the ten martyrs), and from this verse the allusion to them begins. Therefore you will find that he mentioned 'the men' ten times in the parashah, as I shall explain at the end of the parashah, with the help of the Name, may He be exalted."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:19:59.919187362Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}